{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.78,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "wrong_rating",
      "components": ["D1", "T6", "U2", "U3", "U9", "U11"],
      "pins": ["D1.1", "D1.2", "T6.1", "T6.2", "U2.3", "U3.22", "U9.22", "U11.22"],
      "nets": ["/+24V_F", "GND", "+24V"],
      "observed": "D1 is an SMBJ28A TVS from /+24V_F to GND; its component description gives a 45.4 V clamp. That input rail feeds T6 and the board's +24V rail, which supplies the TPS62933 input and the TMC2209 motor-supply pins.",
      "expected": "The input transient protection should limit the rail below the maximum input ratings of the downstream parts. The TPS62933 is a 30 V-input device and the TMC2209 has a 29 V motor-supply maximum; a TVS with a 45.4 V clamp does not protect them against surges that reach its specified clamp level.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"D1\") (value \"28V\") ... (description \"TVS Diode 28VWM 45.4V Clamp 13.2A Ipp Tvs Diode Surface Mount SMB\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"6\") (name \"/+24V_{F}\") ... (node (ref \"D1\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"C\")) ... (node (ref \"T6\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"S\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"3\") (name \"+24V\") ... (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"3\") (pinfunction \"VIN\")) ... (node (ref \"U3\") (pin \"22\") (pinfunction \"VS\")) ... (node (ref \"U9\") (pin \"22\") (pinfunction \"VS\")) ... (node (ref \"U11\") (pin \"22\") (pinfunction \"VS\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"U2\") (value \"TPS62933\") ... (field (name \"PN\") \"TPS62933DRLR\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"U3\") (value \"TMC2209\") ... (field (name \"PN\") \"TMC2209-LA-T\"))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "An input surge large enough to drive the TVS toward its clamp voltage can put the buck regulator and stepper-driver supply pins above their ratings, risking damage or failure despite the presence of the TVS.",
      "confidence": 0.78
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The 24 V input TVS has a specified clamp voltage substantially above the maximum supply ratings of downstream ICs. It may therefore fail to protect the buck regulator and stepper drivers during sufficiently large input transients."
}

